class.description:
An [SQLiteStatement] is compiled once with [method SQLiteDatabase.prepare] and can then be bound and run many times, which is faster than passing the same SQL to [method SQLiteDatabase.execute] again and again.
[codeblock]
var insert = db.prepare("INSERT INTO items (name, weight) VALUES (?1, ?2);")
for item in items:
	insert.bind_text(1, item.name)
	insert.bind_float(2, item.weight)
	insert.step()
	insert.reset()

var select = db.prepare("SELECT name, weight FROM items;")
while select.step() == SQLiteStatement.STEP_RESULT_ROW:
	print(select.get_column_text(0), " ", select.get_column_float(1))
[/codeblock]
Parameter indices start at [code]1[/code] (as in SQL's [code]?1[/code]), column indices start at [code]0[/code]. Errors are reported through the [enum Error] return values and [method SQLiteDatabase.get_last_error_message] of the database. A statement keeps its database object alive, but stops working when the database is closed.
